00:13:17,520 --> 00:13:21,520
I want all hands setting the cradle
the ship comes up in 20 minutes!

255
00:13:21,640 --> 00:13:23,620
We've got salvaging to do!

256
00:13:23,860 --> 00:13:25,360
Aye, aye, Captain!

257
00:13:39,680 --> 00:13:41,740
Okay, he's waving at us!

258
00:13:41,920 --> 00:13:43,417
Smile and wave back, I guess.

259
00:13:43,500 --> 00:13:44,330
Just act normal!

260
00:13:44,413 --> 00:13:45,243
Oh, help!

261
00:13:45,326 --> 00:13:46,200
Doing my best.

262
00:13:46,800 --> 00:13:48,557
Don't get stage-fried, fellas.

263
00:13:48,640 --> 00:13:49,470
They're observers.

264
00:13:49,553 --> 00:13:52,991
They want to see something new,
so show them how it's done.

265
00:13:53,160 --> 00:13:56,866
If you're still nervous, try
picturing them in their underwear.

266
00:13:58,460 --> 00:13:59,840
Drop the cradle!

267
00:14:00,360 --> 00:14:01,190
Aye, aye!

268
00:14:04,600 --> 00:14:07,140
Keep your eyes peeled for those intruders!

269
00:14:07,500 --> 00:14:08,480
Aye, aye, sir!

270
00:14:09,260 --> 00:14:12,297
These guys really take their
salvaging seriously, don't they?

271
00:14:12,380 --> 00:14:15,537
I think they're showing off because
their captain has a crush on me.

272
00:14:15,620 --> 00:14:16,450
Move it, man!

273
00:14:16,540 --> 00:14:17,834
I want this done fast!

274
00:14:18,240 --> 00:14:19,260
All right, sir!

275
00:14:43,140 --> 00:14:46,160
Oh, my God.

276
00:15:31,940 --> 00:15:33,600
Saru, look.

277
00:15:58,820 --> 00:16:00,585
Cradle set is locked in place.

278
00:16:03,600 --> 00:16:04,660
What was that?

279
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:10,240
Ah, so why such a big monkey?

280
00:16:10,480 --> 00:16:12,245
There, on the bow of the ship.

281
00:16:12,380 --> 00:16:13,600
Oh, that!

282
00:16:14,860 --> 00:16:15,840
You like?

283
00:16:15,960 --> 00:16:17,784
It's a special prow I designed.

284
00:16:18,040 --> 00:16:19,117
It ain't in our salvage.

285
00:16:19,200 --> 00:16:20,030
Just watch.

286
00:16:21,120 --> 00:16:22,980
You're gonna love this.

287
00:16:23,540 --> 00:16:25,140
Lower the Brook, hunter!

288
00:16:25,700 --> 00:16:26,880
Aye, aye, sir!

289
00:16:42,380 --> 00:16:43,640
Wow, awesome!

290
00:16:43,940 --> 00:16:46,140
Completely amazing! Are you kidding?

291
00:16:49,060 --> 00:16:50,800
Forty meters to the target.

292
00:16:51,940 --> 00:16:53,240
Thirty meters.

293
00:16:54,820 --> 00:16:55,650
Twenty.

294
00:16:56,960 --> 00:16:57,790
Ten.

295
00:16:59,800 --> 00:17:01,280
Brook hunter joint.

296
00:17:01,960 --> 00:17:02,790
Locked.

297
00:17:03,240 --> 00:17:04,070
Excellent!

298
00:17:04,300 --> 00:17:06,006
Now it's time for me to blow!

299
00:17:09,040 --> 00:17:10,920
Wait, there's no way.

300
00:17:15,380 --> 00:17:18,909
He's actually going to use his
breath to bring up that ship?

301
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:21,340
That's ridiculous!

302
00:17:34,720 --> 00:17:36,280
Is that a bubble?

303
00:17:45,180 --> 00:17:47,880
The body of the ship is off the floor!

304
00:17:49,260 --> 00:17:51,100
All right, howlera!

305
00:17:51,860 --> 00:17:53,040
Aye, aye, sir!

306
00:17:54,580 --> 00:17:55,860
That's hustle, men!

307
00:17:56,140 --> 00:17:57,340
Send more air!

308
00:17:57,760 --> 00:17:59,020
Aye, aye, sir!

309
00:18:08,560 --> 00:18:11,620
Captain, there's a problem
with the underwater crew!

310
00:18:12,240 --> 00:18:13,070
What?

311
00:18:13,153 --> 00:18:14,000
Talk to me!

312
00:18:14,180 --> 00:18:15,827
What's happening down there?

313
00:18:16,040 --> 00:18:18,100
Is it the intruders? Yes, sir!

314
00:18:18,300 --> 00:18:19,476
They're in the ship!

315
00:18:25,680 --> 00:18:28,720
How dare you lay a hand
on my hard-working men?

316
00:18:30,020 --> 00:18:30,850
Intruders!

317
00:18:37,020 --> 00:18:39,877
Uh, you know, we're not going to
take your picture or anything.

318
00:18:39,960 --> 00:18:40,790
You're not?

319
00:18:40,873 --> 00:18:42,800
He was giving us a photo op?

320
00:18:43,060 --> 00:18:43,900
Help us!

321
00:18:44,040 --> 00:18:45,840
Someone please help us!

322
00:18:46,580 --> 00:18:48,060
I'll be right down!

323
00:18:48,400 --> 00:18:50,557
Continue with the
salvaging operation, men!

324
00:18:50,640 --> 00:18:51,680
Aye, sir!

325
00:19:17,120 --> 00:19:18,520
The salvage looks good.

326
00:19:22,700 --> 00:19:23,560
Check it out.

327
00:19:23,780 --> 00:19:25,839
We don't even need the barrels now.

328
00:19:26,180 --> 00:19:29,317
Well, I don't know how they pumped
this much air into a downed ship.

329
00:19:29,400 --> 00:19:31,457
But what I really want
to know is who they are

330
00:19:31,540 --> 00:19:33,377
and why they're trying
to salvage this thing.

331
00:19:33,460 --> 00:19:37,057
I wonder if something bad happened
to Nami and Robin up on the surface.

332
00:19:37,140 --> 00:19:39,964
I've tried calling them,
but they won't respond.

333
00:19:40,180 --> 00:19:42,240
Who do you guys think you are?

334
00:19:42,740 --> 00:19:44,780
Trying to muscle in on my turf?

335
00:19:48,740 --> 00:19:49,620
Nice makeup.

336
00:19:50,560 --> 00:19:53,619
Thanks, I feel it adds a
refined quality to my face.

337
00:19:53,820 --> 00:19:55,597
Oh yeah, certainly adds something.

338
00:19:55,680 --> 00:19:57,417
What the hell are you talking about?

339
00:19:57,500 --> 00:19:58,500
What do you mean?

340
00:19:58,920 --> 00:20:00,977
What he means to say is who are you?

341
00:20:01,060 --> 00:20:02,766
You're right, how rude of me.

342
00:20:02,900 --> 00:20:05,457
Sometimes I get caught up
in the details of life.

343
00:20:05,540 --> 00:20:07,037
It's one of my shortcomings.

344
00:20:07,120 --> 00:20:09,591
Come on, just tell us who you are already.

345
00:20:13,100 --> 00:20:15,100
There's something else down there!

346
00:20:15,560 --> 00:20:16,500
It's huge!

347
00:20:17,420 --> 00:20:18,891
Anybody just want to run?

348
00:20:23,880 --> 00:20:27,821
Yeah, all you guys from the East
Blue have the best sense of humor.

349
00:20:28,180 --> 00:20:29,977
Well, I don't really know about all that.

350
00:20:30,060 --> 00:20:32,677
Nothing compares to a
one-ton gorilla in makeup.

351
00:20:32,760 --> 00:20:33,936
Oh, shut your mouth.

352
00:20:34,100 --> 00:20:35,335
You know I look good.

353
00:20:56,120 --> 00:21:00,440
Does anyone else see the monster the
size of an island in front of us?
